{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1489695-decades-and-atmosphere-in-cofd","id":1489695,"title":"Decades and Atmosphere in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-10T18:24:31-07:00","id":1489695,"title":"Decades and Atmosphere in CofD","content":"So in a recent conversation with some friends, I mentioned how I felt that Mage the Awakening had a strong mood and atmosphere of the late 90s and 2000s for many different reasons(which I quite like).<br /> This started a discussion about how contemporaneous the CofD felt, with some of them thinking our changeling game felt very contemporaneous while others felt like the entirety of CofD felt like a piece of 2000s media.<br /> What do you all think of it? Does CofD 2e still bear a lot of the stylistic feel of the 2000s or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:17:43-07:00","id":1489703,"title":"","content":"The 2e games I've seen (Mage and Changeling in some depth; Hunter, Promethean, Werewolf, and Vampire skimmed) put me in mind of being in 2010 or later. Granted, a large part of that is because I graduated highschool in 2013. Living like an independent adult goes a long way to shaping your worldview, which influences worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> At any rate, working off the assumption that CoD is a bleaker version of our world, most of it lines up. Quality control and standardization is probably less heavily enforced, so tech and safety isn't quite as good as ours. People are poorer, health is worse, and infrastructure is shoddy. All of those make for a borderline dystopia, giving life to our bleakness perceptions of the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-10-2022, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:37:00-07:00","id":1489706,"title":"","content":"2e? Heck no. 2e is so strongly a product of the 2010's it's ridiculous. In particular, it's very emblematic of the early to mid 2010s it came out in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T03:14:39-07:00","id":1489726,"title":"","content":"Not really. Like, I find from the Revised era of WoD, everything feels more or less modern.<br /> <br /> The only real dated stuff I've found has been the Boston chapter in the Promethian chronicle, and certain ideas in <i>Seers of the Throne</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T05:22:36-07:00","id":1489734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LunaLupa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1489695-decades-and-atmosphere-in-cofd#post1489695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in a recent conversation with some friends, I mentioned how I felt that Mage the Awakening had a strong mood and atmosphere of the late 90s and 2000s for many different reasons(which I quite like).<br /> This started a discussion about how contemporaneous the CofD felt, with some of them thinking our changeling game felt very contemporaneous while others felt like the entirety of CofD felt like a piece of 2000s media.<br /> What do you all think of it? Does CofD 2e still bear a lot of the stylistic feel of the 2000s or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vibes we got from the 2nd ed and the feeling we have playing them, give us a strong modern and very horror and dark mood honestly. Coming from the classic wod, for us the 90's feeling is something of the wod not from the cofd. <br /> For us the modern vibes, combined with the fact the the cod cults/clans/tribes are extremely &quot;realistic&quot; and with their own culture and possibly personalized tradition, is so cool that we created our own version of the 5th edition wod especially for werewolf and mage, which are both too strongly tied to human cultures. <br /> <br /> COD vibes are , for me, the diamond of the whole wod/nwod stuff. A perfect compromise for creative minds and at the same time solid bases and borders to identify the various shades between tribes/clans ecc and the kind of game you wanna play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T19:35:15-07:00","id":1489987,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's pretty adaptable, I've never seen it as a product of a specific time period. My Mage game was set in the 1920s. Honestly, I feel like Mage really benefits from a lack of cell phones and computers. That way there is nothing to compete with the information gathering, mystery solving powers of a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T09:39:54-07:00","id":1490264,"title":"","content":"Less about the vibes of the game itself, and the more the vibes of the show, but \u201cGotham\u201d is my group\u2019s new favorite default setting for CofD. Just this delightful mishmash of clothing, tech, and architecture: the bank has a row of clerks using polished brass typewriters, and then someone has a cell phone; high society parties have both regency era ballgowns and sequin minidresses - in the same glamour shot. The car chase is between a 1930\u2019s Rolls Royce and a some one with a trench coat on a Yakima. \u201cThe Past\u201d is always 1923, even if the characters haven\u2019t noticeably aged. And you just goggle over \u201cWhat decade is it?!?\u201d<br /> All of them. It is simultaneously 2010s, 90\u2019s, 80\u2019s 70\u2019s and 50\u2019s, and even 2020. In the most delightful aesthetic, and most plot-convenient explanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 08-15-2022, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T11:49:11-07:00","id":1490725,"title":"","content":"Never really felt like CofD games were dated or emanated the vibes of a specific decade, specially after dark eras 1 &amp; 2 e the fact that later books proposed the use of historic and futuristic settings (Geist, Mummy and Vampire's Guide to the Night) I ended up feeling like CofD it's very adaptable, and that to me it doesn't really shows any specific decade vibe, not the 00's nor de 10's.<br /> <br /> Also I suppose that teh fact that I'm Brazilian and that most of the earlier books used settings at the USA and Europe kinda gave me this slight disconection from a lot of the settings (not getting specific lingo, or cultural references/imagery particular from each decade) helped me have an easier time abstracting these decade markers - since 00's and 10's USA and Europe are VERY different from 00's and 10's Brazil (does that make any sense? anyways, glad that later down the line we've seen a lot of diverse settings outside the Europe/USA ones,;I love it).<br /> <br /> I've seen some posts here saying there are lots of 10's vibes and that might be very true and I'm just not realizing it since I played A LOT of RPG on the 2010's as a young adult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T07:46:02-07:00","id":1491300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1489695-decades-and-atmosphere-in-cofd?p=1489706#post1489706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e? Heck no. 2e is so strongly a product of the 2010's it's ridiculous. In particular, it's very emblematic of the early to mid 2010s it came out in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind expanding on what makes something emblematic of that era in particular? I lived through it, but I wasn't too observant on a broad scale at that time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T10:39:06-07:00","id":1491783,"title":"","content":"New World of Darkness was a collection of games that I saw as very post 9-11. There's a cynicism for authority that is more based in visible excesses rather than the general counter-culture rebelliousness of the 90s/Classic World of Darkness, a different sense of the world being crushing and scary without the benefit of feeling grandiose for standing against that, and it induces a certain freeform, experimental attitude. <br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is something that I see as having been that with a bit more worldly experience (and a bit of a post-recession sort of collection of games). The same worldviews matured a bit, less visceral but more nuanced, with greater critical awareness of ongoing harmful systems (and the ways that their most violent regressiveness means that your posturing cynicism isn't really a good look anymore), and more of an eye towards marginalized voices and helping them to be heard more.<br /> <br /> Classic World of Darkness featured people you'd find on the contemporary club scene, New World of Darkness featured people you'd find in contemporary college campuses, Chronicles of Darkness is those people after they've been struggling on the job market for a while and listening to the news more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T13:27:30-07:00","id":1491808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1489695-decades-and-atmosphere-in-cofd?p=1491783#post1491783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New World of Darkness was a collection of games that I saw as very post 9-11. There's a cynicism for authority that is more based in visible excesses rather than the general counter-culture rebelliousness of the 90s/Classic World of Darkness, a different sense of the world being crushing and scary without the benefit of feeling grandiose for standing against that, and it induces a certain freeform, experimental attitude.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is something that I see as having been that with a bit more worldly experience (and a bit of a post-recession sort of collection of games). The same worldviews matured a bit, less visceral but more nuanced, with greater critical awareness of ongoing harmful systems (and the ways that their most violent regressiveness means that your posturing cynicism isn't really a good look anymore), and more of an eye towards marginalized voices and helping them to be heard more.<br /> <br /> Classic World of Darkness featured people you'd find on the contemporary club scene, New World of Darkness featured people you'd find in contemporary college campuses, Chronicles of Darkness is those people after they've been struggling on the job market for a while and listening to the news more.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fantastic way to think about it and look back at the those older books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}